#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kmyapplication; Handbook"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:64 index.docbook:295
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kmyapplication; is a tool for large scale sample acquisition."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using &kmyapplication; multiple teams can gather training data from "
"potential end users or professional speakers and collect them on the central "
"SSCd server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid "Like Simon / Simond, &kmyapplication; is a client to the SSCd server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kmyapplication; will collect samples through training procedures and send "
"them to the SSCd server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The system also collects useful metadata to the samples like names (or "
"aliases) of the recorded people, their speaking niveau, possible "
"impairments, etc. Information about the used recording equipment is also "
"stored. This and other information is stored on the server side in a "
"database. Please refer to the <ulink url=\"help:/sscd\">SSCd manual</ulink> "
"for more information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For more information on the architecture of the Simon suite please see the "
"<ulink url=\"help:/Simon/overview.html#architecture\">Simon manual</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &kmyapplication;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kmyapplication; provides a simple graphical interface for collecting "
"training samples and managing speakers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:88 index.docbook:280
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Main window</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:94 index.docbook:286
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Main window</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To use SSC connect to the SSCd by pressing <guibutton>Connect</guibutton>. "
"As soon as you are connected, the user interface will allow you to manage "
"users and institutions and record new samples."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To proceed without connecting to the SSCd, you may use the <link linkend="
"\"offline_mode\">offline mode</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To collect samples for a user, simply enter the id of the user in the "
"<guilabel>User ID</guilabel> input field and press <guibutton>Select</"
"guibutton>. The user information will be fetched from the database (SSCd) "
"and the name of the user displayed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid "Managing users"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Before you can record samples from a new speaker you need to add a new user "
"to the system."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add, edit and remove users, select the <guibutton>Manage users</"
"guibutton> option from the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Manage users</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Manage users</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:128
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you see a list of all existing speakers in the database. For "
"performance reason the list <emphasis>may not be complete</emphasis>. To "
"find users in large deployments you can apply filters to the result set by "
"filling out the mask above and pressing <guibutton>Apply Filters</"
"guibutton>. The default is no filter. Empty fields are ignored when "
"filtering."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To filter for a specific institution enter the institution id into the "
"<guilabel>Institution</guilabel> field. If you don't know the institution id "
"by hard you can use the <guibutton>Search</guibutton> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add, edit or remove users simply press the buttons <guibutton>Add</"
"guibutton>, <guibutton>Edit</guibutton> and <guibutton>Remove</guibutton>, "
"respectively."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Add user</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add a user press <guibutton>Add</guibutton> and fill out the presented "
"form."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Add user</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Add user</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:155
#, no-c-format
msgid "Associating with an institution"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Often institutions give unique ids to each patient to reference them in "
"their computer system. &kmyapplication; can be configured to use those "
"institution ids instead of the internal SSCd identifiers. To connect a SSC "
"user to the institution id add a new institution connection to the user by "
"pressing <guibutton>Add</guibutton> below <guilabel>Institution(s):</"
"guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>New institution association</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>New institution association</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:172
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Simply enter the id of the institution the identifier originates from (you "
"may want to use the <guibutton>Search</guibutton> to find institution ids) "
"and the id that identifies the user in that institution."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For example: The speaker \"Jack Jones\" is currently a patient in "
"institution #1. There he is patient \"#520f\". You can then add an "
"institution association associating the speaker \"Jack Jones\" (internal "
"SSCd id \"7\") with the institution \"1\" and institution id \"520f\". If "
"&kmyapplication; is the configured to use institution specific ids of "
"institution \"1\" you can refer to \"Jack Jones\" by using the id \"520f\" "
"instead of \"7\"."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid "Capabilities"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:179
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the speaker is not able to answer interview questions or repeat words "
"spoken by the facilitator then you can let &kmyapplication; know about it by "
"unchecking <guibutton>Interview possible</guibutton> and / or "
"<guibutton>Repeat possible</guibutton>. The unchecked training modes (Repeat "
"and Interview) will then no longer be available for this speaker."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid "Edit user"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To edit a user, simply select the user from the list in the <link linkend="
"\"manage_users\">manage users dialog</link> and press <guibutton>Edit</"
"guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:186
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The interface for editing the user is identical to the interface for <link "
"linkend=\"add_users\">adding a new user</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remove user"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To remove a user, simply select <guibutton>Remove</guibutton> after "
"selecting the user from the list in the <link linkend=\"manage_users"
"\">manage users dialog</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:193
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When removing a user, all associated samples of this speaker will be lost."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:198
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Manage institutions</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kmyapplication; can organize speakers in \"institutions\". Those might be "
"virtual institutions like groups but was originally designed to keep track "
"of hospital and rehabilitation patients. One user can be in zero, one or "
"many institutions."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add, edit and remove institutions select <guibutton>Manage institutions</"
"guibutton> from the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:204
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Manage institutions</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Manage institutions</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When removing institutions, the <link linkend=\"institution_association"
"\">associations to users</link> will be lost, the users however will not be "
"removed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:219
#, no-c-format
msgid "Collecting samples"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:220
#, no-c-format
msgid "To collect samples of a user, there are three training types:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid "Repeat"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"During repeating, the facilitator reads out a word that the user tries to "
"repeat."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid "Training"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:227
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The user reads the text from the screen. In practice the facilitator can "
"read it out for the user to repeat as well."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:230
#, no-c-format
msgid "Interview"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"During the interview the facilitator asks the user a couple of questions and "
"record the answers."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:237
#, no-c-format
msgid "Setting up training material"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Before you can use SSC you will likely want to adjust the training prompts "
"for the recordings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:239
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"They are three, one for each training type, simple text files containing one "
"line per prompt. The encoding is UTF-8."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid "Their location depends on your operation system:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:241
#, no-c-format
msgid "Training data files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:247
#, no-c-format
msgid "Microsoft Windows"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: entry
#: index.docbook:248
#, no-c-format
msgid "GNU/Linux"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: index.docbook:253
#, no-c-format
msgid "%installation folder%\\texts\\"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: index.docbook:254
#, no-c-format
msgid "`kde4-config --install data`/ssc/texts/"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:260
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The path for GNU/Linux uses an inline command to resolve the installation "
"folder for you. You can also run <command>kde4-config --install data</"
"command> in a shell to find out the exact path. On Microsoft Windows you "
"have to fill in the installation folder for yourself. Usually this will be "
"something like <filename>C:\\Program files\\simon 0.3\\</filename> or "
"similar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:263
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <filename>texts</filename> folder will contain three subfolders "
"containing the prompts:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: index.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid "repeat"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: index.docbook:268
#, no-c-format
msgid "<filename>training</filename>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: index.docbook:269
#, no-c-format
msgid "interview"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:274
#, no-c-format
msgid "The training"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:276
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To launch a training session, simply press the appropriate button for your "
"training type in the SSC main window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:292
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To do this you must either be connected to the server or use the <link "
"linkend=\"offline_mode\">offline mode</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When starting the training, you will have the option to use the power "
"training mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:301
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Training: Intro</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:307
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Training: Intro</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:312
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In power training mode samples will start to be recording as soon as the "
"associated prompt is displayed. You can then proceed to the next page simply "
"by pressing <guibutton>Next</guibutton> in the wizard. When you do that the "
"current recording will be stored, written and the next sample will start "
"recording."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:313
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Using the power training option an averagely proficient speaker can complete "
"the training process much quicker. However, because you don't have a break "
"between individual prompts it might be more taxing for the speaker."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:314
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Of course the power training is not an option when letting the speaker "
"repeat what the facilitator says as the latter will invariably be heard on "
"the created recordings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid "Device information"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:318
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this page of the wizard you can provide information about the used "
"hardware devices (soundcard and microphone)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:321
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Training: Device Information</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:327
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Training: Device Information</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:332
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Please enter the model and type of the sound card in the <guilabel>Model</"
"guilabel> and <guilabel>Type</guilabel> fields. Enter the information about "
"the microphone in the two input boxes below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:333
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The drop down boxes are filled with the current list of makes and models "
"from already recorded samples. Before entering a new device please make sure "
"that the same device, maybe named a little bit differently, doesn't already "
"exist to avoid duplicates."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:337
#, no-c-format
msgid "Volume calibration"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:339
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Before the recording starts, &kmyapplication; will try to make sure that the "
"microphone volume(s) are correctly configured."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Training: Volume</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:349
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Training: Volume</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:355
#, no-c-format
msgid "To calibrate simply read the text displayed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:357
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The calibration will monitor the current volume and tell you to either raise "
"or lower the volume but you have to do that manually in your systems audio "
"mixer. Once you changed the volume in any way (while the calibration is "
"running), press the <guibutton>Volume changed</guibutton> button next to the "
"affected device. This will reset the volume status."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:360
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"During calibration, try to talk normally. Don't yell but don't be overly "
"quiet either. Take into account that you should generally use the same "
"volume setting for all your training and for the recognition too. You might "
"speak a little bit louder (unconsciously) when you are upset or at another "
"time of the day so try to raise your voice a little bit to anticipate this. "
"It is much better to have a little quieter samples than to start clipping."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:362
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the &kmyapplication; settings, both the text displayed and the levels "
"considered correct can be changed. If you leave the text empty, the default "
"text will be displayed. In the options you can also deactivate the "
"calibration completely. See the <link linkend=\"configuring_ssc"
"\">configuration section</link> for more details."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:365
#, no-c-format
msgid "Recording data"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:366
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For each line in your <link linkend=\"files\">prompts file</link> you will "
"get one page asking you to record a sample."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:369
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Training: Record</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:375
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Training: Record</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:382
#, no-c-format
msgid "Storing or transmitting data"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:383
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After you recorded the prompts (you may skip prompts at any time) you can "
"upload the collected samples to the server or store them locally to send "
"them later on."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:386
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Training: Transmit</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:392
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Training: Transmit</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:397
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To upload stored samples please refer to the <link linkend=\"stored_samples"
"\">next section</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:403
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Stored samples</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:404
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you don't have a connection to the server or simply don't want to upload "
"the samples right away, you get the option to store samples locally instead "
"of sending them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:405
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is not intended as permanent storage but rather as a intermediate "
"location before you can send the samples to the server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:407
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To access (and upload) stored samples, select <guibutton>Upload stored data</"
"guibutton> from the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:411
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>Stored samples</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:417
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Stored samples</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:423
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The list contains all locally stored training sessions. Each session is "
"identified by the user id (first) and the exact date and time it was "
"recorded (second)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:426
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When recording in <link linkend=\"offline_mode\">offline mode</link> the "
"system doesn't know what user ids do exist. As such you have to either know "
"the correct user id or guess."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:428
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Before uploading the sample, you can change the previously set user id by "
"clicking <guibutton>Edit user</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:430
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you press <guibutton>Upload</guibutton>, the training session will be "
"restored and you get the possibility to hear / re-record all the training "
"samples again before sending them to the server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:432
#, no-c-format
msgid "Once uploaded, the samples are removed from the local computer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:438
#, no-c-format
msgid "Offline mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:439
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kmyapplication; is a <link linkend=\"introduction\">server / client "
"solution</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:441
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Most of the time when working with &kmyapplication; you will want to connect "
"to the server to access the remotely stored database containing users, "
"institutions, etc. When recording samples you will also transfer them to the "
"server directly in most cases."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:443
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sometimes, though, you might not have a (trusted) internet connection "
"available and still need to record samples with &kmyapplication;. For this "
"purpose &kmyapplication; contains an offline mode allowing you to gather "
"speech data without a connection to the SSCd server."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:445
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In offline mode you cannot add, edit or view users or institutions. You can "
"only gather new samples to send to the server later on through the <link "
"linkend=\"stored_samples\">stored samples</link> functionality."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:447
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Recording works the same in offline mode as it does when connected to the "
"server but certain features might be unavailable (like resolving the name or "
"validity of the entered user id)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:451
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring &kmyapplication;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:452
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In &kmyapplication;s configuration you can configure the server to connect "
"to and set up some basic parameters. The audio configuration for the "
"recordings can also be changed here."
msgstr ""

